  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{De Morgan's Laws for Logic}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "Theorem:\ngiven: P, Q is \\\\statement\nthen:\n. \\not{P \\.and./ Q} \\.iff./ (\\not{P} \\.or./ \\not{Q})\n. \\not{P \\.or./ Q} \\.iff./ (\\not{P} \\.and./ \\not{Q})\nDocumented:\n. called: \"De Morgan's Laws for Logic\"\n. description: \"Negation interchanges conjunction and disjunction: $\\neg(P \\land Q)\n                \\iff (\\neg P \\lor \\neg Q)$ and $\\neg(P \\lor Q) \\iff (\\neg P \\land \\neg Q)$.\"\nId: \"e4c6ef38-dd37-448b-a1f5-377df32138ce\"",
